# Bot smoke — checks bot mode itself, not a scenario.
#
# Safe to run anywhere: no /reset, nothing created, no model calls, so it
# finishes in seconds and leaves the installation as it found it. Use it to
# check that the driver types, waits, captures and hands the terminal back
# before trusting a real scenario to it. On an empty installation the reads
# say so and the capture falls back to its placeholder, which is itself the
# behaviour worth seeing.
#
#   npm run ui bot bot-smoke
@note Reading the installation. Nothing here creates or changes anything.
/overview
/functions
@cap WORKER {Worker\s+([A-Za-z][A-Za-z ]+[a-z])}
/tasks
@note The line below carries whatever the capture found, or <worker> if it found nothing.
/chat history "{{WORKER}}"
@wait 2
/workers
/timeline
@note Bot mode reached the end of a plan. The terminal is about to be yours again.
